--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -10,6 +10,12 @@ Each line of an events file is a JSON object:
 
     {"ts": "2024-03-09T23:30:00-05:00", "service": "api", "level": "error", "msg": "upstream timeout"}
 
+To count only recent events, pass `--since` with a date:
+
+    python -m evlog report events.jsonl --since 2024-03-10
+
+This counts events at or after midnight UTC at the start of that day. Timestamps with an offset are compared by the instant they describe, so `2024-03-09T20:00:00-05:00` (01:00 UTC on the 10th) is included. A malformed date, or a missing events file, produces a one-line error instead of a traceback.
+
 Collectors run in several regions and stamp events with their own UTC offset. Legacy collectors (anything installed before 2024) write naive timestamps such as `2024-03-09 22:10:00`; those are UTC. Blank lines are ignored.
 
 Run the tests with `python -m unittest`.
